<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of London (1839)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1839">1839</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of London of 1839 was signed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> and the great powers. It made the Netherlands recognise Belgian independence, nine years after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgian-revolution">Belgian Revolution</a>, divided Limburg and Luxembourg between the two countries and guaranteed Belgium's neutrality. The German invasion of neutral Belgium in 1914 brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-london-1839.jpg" alt="Treaty of London (1839)" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Big Bad Dog · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Belgique_1830.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
